filter-env oracle case: fixture-env-2

Isolates the filter on the second tiny vdb environment in the
fixtures (fixtures/var/db/pkg/dev-libs/infoinstpkg-1.0: CHOST plus
CFLAGS): the captured install-phase pattern (2378 bytes) must leave
both declarations untouched.
If the native port regressed to dropping plain assignments, out
would be short instead of echoing the input.

Run exactly as the phase runtime runs it:
  /usr/bin/python <checkout>/bin/filter-bash-environment.py "$(cat args)" < in > out 2> stderr.txt
Byte-exact: the args file bytes are argv[1] (no trailing newline
added, none present); the in file bytes are stdin verbatim.

Provenance (D4):
  portage-ref: portage-3.0.82.2
  portage-commit: 1d95fc2c552a2c7d347e54093fa0e5b172a57004 (3rdparty/repos.toml [portage] commit)
  python: Python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python)
  input: decompressed fixtures/var/db/pkg/dev-libs/infoinstpkg-1.0/environment.bz2
    with the captured install-phase pattern (2378 bytes,
    byte-identical to captured-phases-install/args) as args.
  sizes: args=2378 in=66 out=66
  date: 2026-10-08 (UTC day granularity; the only field that may change
    between regenerations)
